📦 REQUIRED MODELS — PASTE INTO YOUR RUNPOD TERMINAL
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

# Create folders
mkdir -p /workspace/ComfyUI/models/ultralytics/bbox
mkdir -p /workspace/ComfyUI/models/sams

# Face detector
wget -O /workspace/ComfyUI/models/ultralytics/bbox/face_yolov8m.pt \
  https://huggingface.co/Bingsu/adetailer/resolve/main/face_yolov8m.pt

# Eye detector
wget -O /workspace/ComfyUI/models/ultralytics/bbox/Eyeful_v2-Paired.pt \
  https://huggingface.co/Tenofas/ComfyUI/resolve/main/ultralytics/bbox/Eyeful_v2-Paired.pt

# SAM ViT-B (recommended)
wget -O /workspace/ComfyUI/models/sams/sam_vit_b_01ec64.pth \
  https://dl.fbaipublicfiles.com/segment_anything/sam_vit_b_01ec64.pth
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
🧠 WHAT THE NODES DO
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

The UltralyticsDetectorProvider nodes load AI detection models that find specific things in your image — one detects faces, one detects eyes. They feed into the FaceDetailer which uses SAM (Segment Anything Model) to cleanly mask the detected regions before re-running generation on just those areas.

The BetaSamplingScheduler controls the pacing of the denoising steps — instead of a flat schedule, the alpha/beta parameters let you shape the curve so the model does the right amount of work at the right time for cleaner, sharper results.

